   "text": "MatchmakingPool -> RatingBucketedPool\n    enqueue(player_id, rating, time_control)\n    findCandidates(player_id, rating, window)\n    removeBoth(player_id_a, player_id_b)   # the ATOMIC claim\nChessEngine -> StandardChessRules\n    isLegalMove / applyMove / isCheckmate / isDraw\nMoveLogWriter -> AppendOnlyMoveLog\n    append(game_id, move, ply, ts) / replay(game_id)\nRatingService -> EloRatingService\n    expectedScore(a, b) / update(a, b, result, k)\nSessionRouter -> ConsistentHashSessionRouter\n    assign(game_id) / locate(game_id)\nGameSession   the per-game orchestrator, owning board_state",
   "originalText": "MatchmakingPool -> RatingBucketedPool\n    enqueue(player_id, rating, time_control)\n    findCandidates(player_id, rating, window)\n    removeBoth(player_id_a, player_id_b)   # the ATOMIC claim\nChessEngine -> StandardChessRules\n    isLegalMove / applyMove / isCheckmate / isDraw\nMoveLogWriter -> AppendOnlyMoveLog\n    append(game_id, move, ply, ts) / replay(game_id)\nRatingService -> EloRatingService\n    expectedScore(a, b) / update(a, b, result, k)\nSessionRouter -> ConsistentHashSessionRouter\n    assign(game_id) / locate(game_id)\nGameSession   the per-game orchestrator, owning board_state",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "ifc",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "an2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1000,
   "y": 366,
   "width": 636,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100029,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700203,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Every legality decision in the entire system goes through ONE interface, so a variant\nruleset like Chess960 is a second implementation behind it - never a rewrite of\nGameSession. And MoveLogWriter.replay is used ONLY by the crash-recovery and\nreconnection paths, never by the hot move-validation path.",
   "originalText": "Every legality decision in the entire system goes through ONE interface, so a variant\nruleset like Chess960 is a second implementation behind it - never a rewrite of\nGameSession. And MoveLogWriter.replay is used ONLY by the crash-recovery and\nreconnection paths, never by the hot move-validation path.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
