  },
  {
   "id": "mv_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 886,
   "width": 924,
   "height": 270,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100056,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700392,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "GameSession.onMove(player_id, client_seq, from, to, promotion):\n    if client_seq <= lastAppliedSeq[player_id]:\n        return currentState()          # retried/duplicate - safe NO-OP\n\n    if player_id != board_state.turn_player:\n        raise IllegalMove('not your turn')\n    if not chessEngine.isLegalMove(board_state, from, to, promotion):\n        raise IllegalMove('illegal move')\n\n    board_state = chessEngine.applyMove(board_state, move)\n    lastAppliedSeq[player_id] = client_seq\n    moveLogWriter.append(game_id, move, ply, now())        # async\n\n    broadcastToBothPlayers('move.applied', board_state, move)\n\n    if chessEngine.isCheckmate(board_state) or isDraw(board_state):\n        endGame(result=...)            # -> RatingService.update(...)\n    return board_state",
   "originalText": "GameSession.onMove(player_id, client_seq, from, to, promotion):\n    if client_seq <= lastAppliedSeq[player_id]:\n        return currentState()          # retried/duplicate - safe NO-OP\n\n    if player_id != board_state.turn_player:\n        raise IllegalMove('not your turn')\n    if not chessEngine.isLegalMove(board_state, from, to, promotion):\n        raise IllegalMove('illegal move')\n\n    board_state = chessEngine.applyMove(board_state, move)\n    lastAppliedSeq[player_id] = client_seq\n    moveLogWriter.append(game_id, move, ply, now())        # async\n\n    broadcastToBothPlayers('move.applied', board_state, move)\n\n    if chessEngine.isCheckmate(board_state) or isDraw(board_state):\n        endGame(result=...)            # -> RatingService.update(...)\n    return board_state",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "mv",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1000,
   "y": 886,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 45,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100057,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700399,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The turn_player check happening BEFORE legality, not after, is deliberate: an\nout-of-turn move should never even reach the more expensive legal-move check. The\ncheapest, most decisive rejection reason comes first.",
   "originalText": "The turn_player check happening BEFORE legality, not after, is deliberate: an\nout-of-turn move should never even reach the more expensive legal-move check. The\ncheapest, most decisive rejection reason comes first.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1000,
   "y": 952,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 45,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100058,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700406,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "And the client_seq guard makes a retried submit a safe no-op rather than a second\nmove - the same idempotency-key shape as everywhere else in this guide, at\nper-connection scope rather than per-payment.",
   "originalText": "And the client_seq guard makes a retried submit a safe no-op rather than a second\nmove - the same idempotency-key shape as everywhere else in this guide, at\nper-connection scope rather than per-payment.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1000,
   "y": 1018,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 105,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100059,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700413,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "GameSession.onMove is the DELIBERATE EXCEPTION to 'push atomicity down into the\nstore'. Because the Session Router pins BOTH players' connections for a given\ngame_id to exactly one instance, there is no second instance that could ever race\nthis method for the same game. A lightweight in-process guard - or simply\nprocessing each game's moves single-threaded, actor-style - is correct and\nsufficient. Reaching for a distributed claim here would be solving a race that\nstructurally cannot happen on this path.",
   "originalText": "GameSession.onMove is the DELIBERATE EXCEPTION to 'push atomicity down into the\nstore'. Because the Session Router pins BOTH players' connections for a given\ngame_id to exactly one instance, there is no second instance that could ever race\nthis method for the same game. A lightweight in-process guard - or simply\nprocessing each game's moves single-threaded, actor-style - is correct and\nsufficient. Reaching for a distributed claim here would be solving a race that\nstructurally cannot happen on this path.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn4",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1000,
   "y": 1148,
   "width": 599,
   "height": 45,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100060,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700420,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "By contrast, removeBoth needs one precisely BECAUSE a language-level mutex would\nonly protect threads on the same instance, and do nothing about a peer instance\nclaiming the same pair a moment later.",
   "originalText": "By contrast, removeBoth needs one precisely BECAUSE a language-level mutex would\nonly protect threads on the same instance, and do nothing about a peer instance\nclaiming the same pair a moment later.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d4",
